{"sourceSha256": "91998b6befa15cbdebbc50284bfa35512627cedc5746a471282992747a6871f0", "text": "OET Sample role-play\nROLEPLAYER CARD NO. 2 NURSING\n\nCommunity Health Centre\n\nYou are visiting your local health centre to obtain information about your mother's\nmost recent health report. Your mother is now eighty years old and is becoming\nsomewhat forgettul. She is a very independent person and does not like your\ninterfering in her personal affairs. However, she told.you recently that when she had\nher three-mnonthly check-up, the doctor said her cholesterol level was fairly high.\nThe purposeof your Visit is to leam more about cholesterol and how best to\nreduce tt.\n\nIf the nurse doesn’t explain it, find out what cholesterol is,\n\nAsk what the doctor meant by a fairy high level of cholesterol. Explain that you\nare concerned that her condition could develop into something worse.\n\nAsk what the nurse considers your mother’s cholesterol level should be.\n\nAsk for advice about whet your mother should do to lower her cholesterol level,\n\n© Cacnbridge Bosnil Language Ausesemert Sample role. ply\n\nOET Sample role-play\n\nCANDIDATE CARD NO. 2 NURSING\nCommunity Health Centre\n\nThe son/daughter of an eighty-year-old woman has come to ask for information\nabout cholesterol. He/she wants information about hisher mother's current\ncholesterol level and how best to reduce It\n\n« Find out whal the son/daughter already knows about cholesterol,\n\n® Inform:your visitor about what cholesterol is (fat-ike material present\nIn the blood and most tissues) and about types of cholesterol (high density\nlipaprotems (HDL) — geod, low density lipoproteins (LDL) — baci),\nTactfully explain that if the fatty deposits are lodged in the arteries, this can lead\nto heart disease or stroke.\n\nExplain what the doctor meant by a fairly high level of cholesterol (.2., devated\nabove 5.5 mmots/litre in the blood).\n\nAdvise your visitor about how his/her mother can best deal with her cho